ation and is never interpolated, averaged or blended between models.","processing":"Thirteen ICON-EU single-level parameters (cape_ml, clch, clcl, clcm, clct, pmsl, relhum_2m, t_2m, t_g, td_2m, tot_prec, vis, ww) are read from one cycle, checked for parameter, surface, units, statistical processing, initialization and valid time, then cropped to 18\u00b0W\u20132\u00b0E / 48\u00b0\u201359\u00b0N on the source 0.0625\u00b0 grid, rows north-to-south and columns west-to-east. Values are converted to the published units and rounded once (0.1 \u00b0C, whole per cent, 0.1 hPa, 0.1 km, 0.1 mm, whole J/kg) and clipped into their plausible range; a value outside it fails the run. precip is derived by differencing tot_prec. Only the declared frameVariables are gridded, because thirteen arrays per frame would be about 3 MB of JSON; spotSeries carries every variable at every published hour, bilinearly sampled except ww, which is read from the containing cell. No hour is interpolated: only native forecast steps are published.","sourceUrl":"https://opendata.dwd.de/weather/nwp/icon-eu/grib/","attribution":"Weather data: Deutscher Wetterdienst (DWD) ICON-EU open data, licensed CC BY 4.0; converted, cropped and processed by Force5 (wingfoil.ie).","licenseUrl":"https://www.dwd.de/EN/service/legal_notice/legal_notice_node.html"}